description:
Enable or disable MCP tools by name. Allows controlling which tools are available for the AI agent.

Argument types — give these arguments as RQL values (as in rql-mutate): {key: value, …}, [a, b], "text", 1.5, true, ref("GameObject#12") from a query result, unity.find("Name"); leave out keys you do not need:
ToolToggleInput {Name string (Name of the MCP tool to enable or disable.), Enabled bool (Whether the tool should be enabled (true) or disabled (false).)}
